# config/llama-server-egpu.env
# Configuration for the llama-server inference backend (egpu slot -- P40 eGPU).
# This file is read by systemd's EnvironmentFile directive.
# Model-specific settings (model path, context window, GPU layers, sampling
# flags) do NOT live here: the manager renders the model's profile into
# /var/lib/llama-manager/egpu.env on every swap.
#
# Deployed at /etc/llama/llama-server-egpu.env with the P40's real UUID (see
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES below); config/manager.env lists `egpu` in SLOTS. See
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-23-dual-gpu-three-slot-design.md Phase 4.

# CUDA device selector. Mirrors config/llama-server.env's DEVICE: CUDA0 names
# an enumeration position, not a card, and is only unambiguous because
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES below restricts this process to exactly one physical
# card. See that file's DEVICE comment and the device-pinning section of
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-23-dual-gpu-three-slot-design.md.
DEVICE=CUDA0

# Restricts this process to the P40 by UUID -- see config/llama-server.env's
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES comment for why an ordinal is not sufficient. Get it
# with:
#   nvidia-smi --query-gpu=uuid,pci.bus_id,name --format=csv
# and pick the row named "Tesla P40" (the other row is the V100, which
# belongs to config/llama-server.env, not this file). Set
# CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=GPU-<that uuid> in the deployed copy of this file at
# /etc/llama/llama-server-egpu.env. Never commit a real UUID here -- it is
# specific to one physical card in one machine. The placeholder below is
# intentionally invalid so this service fails loudly rather than silently
# landing on the wrong card if deployed unedited.
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=GPU-<uuid-of-the-p40-see-comment-above>

# Work around a CUDA-backend leak where CUDA graphs are cached per
# generation and not freed, growing host RAM under sustained load
# (llama.cpp issue #20315). See config/llama-server.env for the same note;
# left enabled here as the conservative choice pending its own remeasurement
# on this slot.
GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS=1

# Bind address and port. Always localhost -- the model manager is the
# public-facing endpoint.
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=8084
